WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:06.200
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie this is my Korra
episode 4 video.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.280
I’ll say probably one of my favorite episodes
of the entire series so far.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:14.610
And it had one of the best animation sequences
on the series so far.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.210
So I’ll start with top 5 moments then do
my review.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:18.410
And new round of the giveaway starts now.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:28.730
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:31.150
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.150
Here we go.

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:38.930
Number 5 - Airbender Mission Impossible

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:43.180
The episode was called the calling, but metaphorically
both the airbender children and Korra couldn’t

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.070
hear the message until they dropped their
baggage.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.440
Thematically the two storyline’s didn’t
sync up quite as much as I thought they could,

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:55.809
but you could view the bag of food as a mirror
for Korra’s metal bits in her body.

00:00:55.809 --> 00:00:59.630
Both the children and Korra had physical and
emotional baggage weighing them down.

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:03.780
The Swamp vines trying to keep them in the
swamp were also a little like the Swamp trying

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.420
to teach Korra a lesson.

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.460
The Swamp is a singular organism which is
really the Banyan Grove Tree, so we should

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.630
say that the Banyan Tree was trying to teach
everyone the lesson.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.810
Meelo’s line about trying to toughen up
Jinora and Meelo was a good way to explain

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.520
the whole arc of the episode.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.700
I was trying to toughen up these ladies but
it was a team effort.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:21.850
The funny thing about that is it makes it
sound like Meelo is a representation of the

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:53.960
Banyan Grove Tree.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.610
Number 4 - Ikki with the Guards

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.370
We were kind of disconnected from what was
going on in the Earth Kingdom so in addition

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:02.770
to just being a funny scene, this also informs
us that Kuvira is marching almost the entire

00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:04.880
army on Zhaofu.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:06.270
I guess that’s going to go down next week.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:12.340
I loved how Ikki turned into this miyazaki-type
precocious little girl winning over the guards.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:16.209
I know it seemed like she wasn’t aware they
wanted to capture korra but that bit at the

00:02:16.209 --> 00:02:20.120
end where she figured out Korra was in the
swamp made me feel like she knew what was

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.560
going on the whole time.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:27.510
One of the things I like about animation in
general, not just anime, is that the children

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.590
are usually smarter than the adults.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.790
South Park is probably the best example but
it seems like the younger you are, the more

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.560
wisdom you get to impart.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:39.280
Like even Korra learns a lot from Jinora who’s
much much younger.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.220
Jinora and Tenzin are probably an even better
comparison.

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:50.019
One of these days I hope they release an Avatar
Map Book.

00:02:50.019 --> 00:02:54.160
Like A Song of Ice And Fire has a big really
mind blowing book of maps.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.879
I want one for Last Airbender and Korra that
just shows different maps based on the different

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:00.250
eras of each Avatar.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:05.120
Or even just a detailed encyclopedia of all
the previous avatars starting with Wan.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.860
Even if it just had their names and a short
sentence about each one.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:09.860
We really only know a lot about a handful
of them.

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:11.480
But when you look at all the statues in the
air temple you can see there have been thousands

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.480
of avatars.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:13.480
It’s been over ten thousand years since
Wan lived.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.480
Number 3 - Story Time with Toph

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:19.780
This was some serious fan service, I threw
some rocks at the avatar, he whined.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.590
What’s there to tell.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:25.560
I love that as toph has gotten older, her
personality has regressed back to what it

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.830
was like during last airbender.

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:31.940
In the Lin flashbacks during Book 3 the middle-aged
toph looked way more serious and burdened

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.380
by all the political aspects of running a
large police force.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:37.720
It totally makes sense that after she dropped
that ball and chain she’d start loosening

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.390
up.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:43.110
Last Airbender Toph always seemed like the
most chill of all the team aang characters.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.290
She still had her own demons to deal with
but she was kind of a hippie.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.400
She refused to wear shoes and she really didn’t
care about most of the big political or social

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:51.400
things going on in the world.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:52.610
She was also the most in-tune with nature.

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:55.890
I think Suyin said that she was the one who
originated Zhaofu, so it’s like Toph was

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:58.860
this very balanced person and one child rebelled
by becoming super hardcore, Lin and the other

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:06.129
child, Suyin, rebelled by going extreme in
the other direction.

00:04:06.129 --> 00:04:07.340
Super new wave hippie.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.580
It makes me feel like Toph is the wisest person
in the avatar universe right now.

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:15.030
She is the only one who is completely balanced.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.970
Number 2 - Korra at the Banyan Grove Tree

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.729
Lots of crying going on for the last 5 minutes
of the episode.

00:04:20.729 --> 00:04:25.410
The Bayan Tree animation was very similar
to the way they animated the last airbender

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.830
scene with Aang seeing through the root system
to find people.

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:29.830
Very nice callback.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:30.830
I’m guessing Jinora wasn’t able to sense
her because her spiritual alignment was so

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:31.830
out of whack.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:32.830
There’s always been something about the
swamp that makes it seem like a spiritual

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:33.830
shield.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:38.300
Like there’s so much spiritual energy crackling
around, individual people are too hard to

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:39.300
pinpoint.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.600
I also loved Toph’s lesson.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:44.639
There’s a saying that goes good and bad
luck always come in three’s which is all

00:04:44.639 --> 00:04:48.090
I could think about when Korra was having
visions of all three of her former enemies.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:50.760
That was a badass animation sequence.

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:53.190
The way they super imposed those moments.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:56.910
I’m wondering if that’s the last time
we’re going to see them.

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:00.660
If Korra got rid of the baggage, then presumably
they’re not rattling around in her head

00:05:00.660 --> 00:05:01.660
anymore.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.389
We typically only see things that Korra is
actively thinking about.

00:05:05.389 --> 00:05:11.530
I know everyone is wondering if we’ll see
the former avatar lives again.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.520
The comics are kind of a backdoor to that.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.840
Bryke said they didn’t want Korra to have
that crutch to lean on in Book 4.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:18.850
But there’s still the possibility that she
could reconnect with them after she resolves

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:19.850
the conflict this season.

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:25.479
and my Number 1 moment - Korra Restores her
Avatar State

00:05:25.479 --> 00:05:28.240
Does anyone else think that Korra is her own
worst enemy.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.039
Like she has almost unlimited power but because
mentally she’s been unable to process what’s

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:35.610
been going on, she pretty much neutralizes
herself.

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:39.889
She did what all those villains were trying
to do to her.

00:05:39.889 --> 00:05:43.370
But she just fixed it so we’re good to go.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:44.370
We can resume the action.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:45.450
The last two episodes were really a break
in the main storyline for her.

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.450
Just wandering around the swamp with Toph.

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:47.450
Korra’s vacation from being the avatar is
over.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:50.169
The metalbending scene was probably the most
beautiful animation I’ve seen on Korra ever.

00:05:50.169 --> 00:05:51.570
And it’s only episode 4.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:54.190
So I’m expecting something even better later
this season.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:56.200
Bryke definitely went all out for these final
episodes.

00:05:56.200 --> 00:06:03.990
I can’t wait to listen to the dvd commentary
and hear what they have to say about the more

00:06:03.990 --> 00:06:07.160
technical aspects of scenes like this.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:13.620
They didn’t say anything about it at comic
con just because it would have been super

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.620
spoilery.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.430
Let me know what your favorite moment was.

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:19.460
And while you think about that here’s some
awesome news.

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:22.949
They did a Q&amp;A session on the Avatar Wiki
yesterday and said there would be lots more

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:27.000
Last Airbender Comics an Korra stuff from
Dark Horse.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.280
No more tv shows of course, but lots more
comics.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:34.520
Dark Horse has been their publisher and they’re
very excited to continue making new comic

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:35.520
stories.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:39.050
So don’t expect new avatars any time soon
but it’s possible after they’ve felt like

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:43.110
they’ve done all the korra stories they
want to do they could introduce a new avatar

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:55.160
in 
the comics.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.330
Overall I gave this episode a B plus.

00:06:57.330 --> 00:07:01.780
The Korra storyline was amazing but I don’t
feel like the Airbender half of the episode

00:07:01.780 --> 00:07:03.300
was as strong.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:14.900
I just don’t think the Korra baggage was
reflected in the baggage the airbenders were

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:16.580
carrying around.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:19.740
Ikki had that line about being left out of
the action.

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.060
Her siblings never inlcude her.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:25.040
That would have rang a little stronger if
it had been something closer to what Korra

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.720
has been going through.

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:32.910
Other people only ever want to include her
in things, she’s the one who purposefully

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:34.180
stepped away.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:36.130
Metaphorically all the beats worked for me
in the episode, they were both great stories

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:38.363
the airbenders and Korra, I just feel like
they could have been in sync a little more.

00:07:38.363 --> 00:07:40.340
Like if they had just made Jinora the center
of the airbender story and explained why she

00:07:40.340 --> 00:07:41.340
was having so much trouble with her spiritual
radar.

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:42.569
So, Q&amp;A tomorrow, be sure to leave all your
questions.

00:07:42.569 --> 00:07:47.290
If you haven’t seen my other videos this
week, Constantine is premiering on NBC tonight

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:48.699
so be sure to check it out.

00:07:48.699 --> 00:07:49.930
It’s going to be a lot of fun.

00:07:49.930 --> 00:07:51.879
It’s one of the new DC Comics tv shows.

00:07:51.879 --> 00:07:54.069
It’s based on the Hellblazer comics.

00:07:54.069 --> 00:07:58.900
I’ll post my review after the episode airs.

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:03.720
Right now click here for the Korra Q&amp;A and
click here for last week’s episode.

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:12.830
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and play some more of the korra game.

